·rehʹ."}]}],"28116":[{"footnoteId":10284,"paragraphs":[{"pid":111,"text":"“Sin.” Gr., ha·mar·tiʹan; Lat., pec·caʹto; J17(Heb.), ha·chetʼʹ, from a root meaning “to miss the mark [as in spear throwing].” See vs 23."}]}],"28125":[{"footnoteId":10285,"paragraphs":[{"pid":112,"text":"The quotations in vss 13-18 are found in Ps 13:3 in LXX. See Ps 14:3 ftn."}]}],"28126":[{"footnoteId":10286,"paragraphs":[{"pid":113,"text":"“The Law.” Gr., ho noʹmos, with the definite article ho to particularize. Here the context warrants capitalization to indicate the “Law” given through Moses. In The Bible Translator, Vol. 1, January 1950, published by The United Bible Societies, London, p. 165, J. Harold Greenlee states: “The word ‘law’ requires individual attention. The [Greek] article indicates a particular law, or the Mosaic law; without the article, reference may be to ‘law’ as a principle.”"}]}],"28129":[{"footnoteId":10287,"paragraphs":[{"pid":114,"text":"“Jesus.” B omits."}]}],"28131":[{"footnoteId":10288,"paragraphs":[{"pid":115,"text":"Or, “through the redemption that is in (by) Christ.”"}]}],"28132":[{"footnoteId":10289,"paragraphs":[{"pid":116,"text":"“An offering for propitiation.” Lit., “propitiatory.” Gr., hi·la·steʹri·on; Lat., pro·pi·ti·a·ti·oʹnem; J17(Heb.), lekhap·poʹreth, “as a propitiatory cover.” See Heb 9:5."}]}],"28135":[{"footnoteId":10290,"paragraphs":[{"pid":117,"text":"Lit., “to be being justified.” Gr., di·kai·ouʹsthai; Lat., iu·sti·fi·caʹri."}]}],"28139":[{"footnoteId":10291,"paragraphs":[{"pid":118,"text":"“Say about Abraham . . . flesh,” B; אADVg, “say that Abraham our forefather according to the flesh has gained.”"}]}],"28141":[{"footnoteId":10292,"paragraphs":[{"pid":119,"text":"See App 1D."}]}],"28142":[{"footnoteId":10293,"paragraphs":[{"pid":120,"text":"Lit., “is being reckoned.” Gr., lo·giʹze·tai; Lat., in·pu·taʹtur."}]}],"28144":[{"footnoteId":10294,"paragraphs":[{"pid":121,"text":"Or, “David also pronounces the felicitation.”"}]}],"28146":[{"footno